    "title": "pandas.api.typing.Resampler.size — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.api.typing.Resampler.size#\n\n- final Resampler.size()[source]#\n- Compute group sizes. This method returns the number of rows in each resampled time period, including rows with missing values. \n  - Returns:\n    - Series\n    - Number of rows in each group.\n See also \n  - `Series.groupby`\n  - Apply a function groupby to a Series.\n  - `DataFrame.groupby`\n  - Apply a function groupby to each row or column of a DataFrame.\n Examples >>> ser = pd.Series( ... [1, 2, 3], ... index=pd.DatetimeIndex([\"2023-01-01\", \"2023-01-15\", \"2023-02-01\"]), ... ) >>> ser 2023-01-01 1 2023-01-15 2 2023-02-01 3 dtype: int64 >>> ser.resample(\"MS\").size() 2023-01-01 2 2023-02-01 1 Freq: MS, dtype: int64",
    "markdown_length": 690,
